{
  "name": "shutdown_hooks",
  "description": "A minimal Rust interface for registering process shutdown hooks by wrapping the C standard library's atexit function. It provides a simplified FFI abstraction to ensure specific cleanup logic is executed during the program's termination sequence, bridging Rust applications with low-level process lifecycle management. The implementation currently supports hook registration with future plans for managed hook removal and collection handling.",
